WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
An ancient Jewish teaching
says: save one life,

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.730
and it is as if you saved a whole world.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.740
So on Shabbat, the day of rest, a Jew
may drive a sick person to hospital.

4
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.520
Saving a life overrides
almost every commandment.

5
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.880
But could the same law ever
allow weapons that kill millions?

6
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.520
In this mission, you'll find the 3 things
Jewish law says a person must never

7
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.240
do, even to save their own life.

8
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.190
Then you'll read the verse
the rabbis use to say:

9
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.580
live by the commandments,
do not die by them.

10
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.060
Your mission: find out how far
the duty to save life reaches,

11
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.280
from Shabbat to the battlefield.
